    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "category": "agreement",
          "claim_id": "sha256:5b9a69aa8f3f618d9523407fb59949cda1d2b00ad059aa24213ddb152c71e0f9",
          "fact_ids": [
            "sha256:1f4cae422bda1de8686013cd77c571cab4a4e690624d359c1727fe29af37a82a",
            "sha256:d22122856762526c755e9c2bcad3a82840211fbfa7a93df3ccb0718f84e192c4",
            "sha256:294f13a74881925f44321bb0e4b6c8779cdb119ee5bea24679b1efca361444c7",
            "sha256:5434ce6e1699830e21d1ba73b6491be9eda33e429518139655e368bf1d8764f7"
          ],
          "text": "The source, Blau Syndrome, and target, Blau syndrome, both describe the condition as involving arthritis and uveitis."
        },
        {
          "category": "difference",
          "claim_id": "sha256:bcd3a967088e8bda4c043827b1f2ec4d79b5c4874b08ae18672950c06bce172a",
          "fact_ids": [
            "sha256:d22122856762526c755e9c2bcad3a82840211fbfa7a93df3ccb0718f84e192c4",
            "sha256:5434ce6e1699830e21d1ba73b6491be9eda33e429518139655e368bf1d8764f7"
          ],
          "text": "Their definition details differ: the source says it is caused by a NOD2 mutation, usually presents before age four, and features granulomatous dermatitis and arthritis with synovitis; the target describes familial granulomatous arthritis and skin granulomas and states a material basis in heterozygous NOD2 mutations."
        }
      ],
